From 3afd74e31d0f0bc921937ba9503b4ab51740e63e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 08:06:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: call them modules, and never lock the founder out
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two things, both reported from the live Lab.

A programme's parts were labelled live sessions everywhere. On a cohort or
a long training they are modules — a unit of a course, with a live class
inside it — so that is what the console, the programme page and the
facilitator's own list now call them. The page listing what is happening
soon is called Live Classes, because that is what it is; its address is
unchanged so existing links still work.

And the super admin tier had a trap in it. The founder held the tier only
while no appointed super admin existed, so appointing a colleague removed
the founder's ability to undo the appointment. That is exactly what
happened, within an hour. The founder — the first staff account — is now
always a super admin, read fresh on every request and written nowhere, and
their role cannot be changed by anyone, including a super admin they
appointed. The console shows it as fixed rather than offering a control
that would be refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
